{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ecommerce API",
    "description": "Ecommerce backend API. Import this one file; no separate environment is needed.\n\n**Before you start:** run the backend (`npm run dev`). For the admin folder, create the first admin with `npm run create-admin`, then set `adminEmail` and `adminPassword` on the collection's Variables tab.\n\n**Automatic:** login and signup requests save `accessToken`, and the refresh token is kept by Postman's cookie jar. Seller profile requests save `sellerProfileId`.\n\n**By hand:** OTP codes print in the server terminal while `EMAIL_DRIVER` and `SMS_DRIVER` are `console`. Copy each into the `otpCode` variable before sending the request that needs it.\n\n**Errors** look like `{ \"message\": \"...\", \"code\": \"...\", \"details\": [...] }`. `code` and `details` are not always present.\n\n**Rate limits** (per IP, all /auth routes): 300 requests per 15 min, 30 failed login or code attempts per 15 min, 20 signups per hour, 20 OTP sends per hour. Over the limit returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After`. Restarting the server resets them.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
